      "sort_scope": "Threshold for uniform net reduction of the entire archived QLI call, allowing the fastest possible propagation and the largest credit across participating ranks per layer. It is not the measured fraction spent sorting. Hold layer-20 candidate block output unchanged; retain the exact ordering of the top 512, including tied and nonfinite values, score scaling and index offsets. Any different tile-select algorithm needs its own numerical and cost evidence. The frozen trace predates the later shared membership implementation.",
      "method": "Single arch22 QLI kernel. Only split-S2 publishes sorted score/ID lists through vec1ResGm and ProcessLD rereads them. Each split row record is at most 4096 32-bit words per direction. Full K output and candidate side output are distinct. Separate score plane uses FP32 Cube result -> Vector input once per query/key. Bound eight actual source calls by real local Q and original kernel durations. Grant all score-plane and/or list traffic exposed, no replacement, at the stated sustained read+write rate, including 4-row and 2048-key padded sensitivity. Does not bound changes to vector sorting, Cube math, internal barriers, parallelism or bandwidth below the model. No inter-kernel launch saved inside QLI; a cross-core replacement needs a valid exchange and unchanged ties.",
      "decision": "deprioritize_two_workspace_transfers_keep_sort_compute_conditional",
      "reopen_if": "Use the per-family break-even threshold for a reduced-width tile-select/merge or another savings beyond workspace traffic."
    },
